"DTMB - Glossary of Printing Terms (https://www.michigan.gov/dtmb/services/print/glossary/glossary-of-printing-terms)\nciteturn4view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view1\",\"lineno\":280}); Total lines: 410\nL0: cite0†Google Tag Manager†www.googletagmanager.com L1: \nL2: cite1†Skip to main content L3: \nL4: cite2†Image: Michigan Header Logo L5: \nL6: DTMB\nL7: \nL8: About Us\nL9: \nL10: cite3†Go to About Us L11: \nL12: Careers\nL13: \nL14: cite4†Go to Careers L15: \nL16: DTMB Careers\nL17: \nL18: Executives\nL19: \nL20: cite5†Go to Executives L21: \nL22: DTMB Executives\nL23: \nL24: Newsroom\nL25: \nL26: cite6†Go to Newsroom L27: \nL28: Law & Policies\nL29: \nL30: cite7†Go to Law & Policies L31: \nL32: Administrative Guide\nL33: \nL34: cite8†Go to Administrative Guide L35: \nL36: The Administrative Guide to State Government presents what an informed person should know about the major processes of state government .\nL37: Boards and Commissions\nL38: \nL39: cite9†Go to Boards and Commissions L40: \nL41: DTMB has multiple Boards and Commissions for which they have administrative oversight.\nL42: \nL43: Reports to the Legislature\nL44: \nL45: cite10†Go to Reports to the Legislature L46: \nL47: DTMB Reports to the Michigan legislature organized by fiscal year\nL48: \nL49: State Administrative Board\nL50: \nL51: cite11†Go to State Administrative Board L52: \nL53: The State Administrative Board has general supervisory control over the administrative activities of all state departments and agencies.\nL54: IT Policies, Standards & Procedures\nL55: \nL56: cite12†Go to IT Policies, Standards & Procedures L57: \nL58: Information technology (IT) Policies document the DTMB's authority to establish Standards and Procedures in the specified areas.\nL59: \nL60: Strategy & Governance\nL61: \nL62: cite13†Go to Strategy & Governance L63: \nL64: At the heart of the DTMB organization are the fundamental governance elements that define the department's authorities, processes, and procedures\nL65: \nL66: Services\nL67: \nL68: cite14†Go to Services L69: \nL70: Archives of Michigan\nL71: \nL72: cite15†Go to Archives of Michigan L73: The Archives of Michigan is responsible for preserving the records of Michigan government and other public institutions. The collections also include documents, maps, photographs and film from private individuals and organizations.\nL74: \nL75: Cybersecurity\nL76: \nL77: cite16†Go to Cybersecurity L78: \nL79: Cybersecurity information for the state of Michigan and resources for the public. Featuring educational and support information for local government, schools and more.\nL80: \nL81: Maps | Geographic Information Systems (GIS)\nL82: cite17†Go to Maps | Geographic Information Systems (GIS) L83: \nL84: The State of Michigan Geographic Information Systems (GIS) and Mapping Site provides access to GIS data, and information across the GIS community in Michigan.\nL85: \nL86: ID Mail and Delivery Services\nL87: \nL88: cite18†Go to ID Mail and Delivery Services L89: \nL90: DTMB Delivery Services provides comprehensive transport services tailored to the needs of each customer as well as ID Mail and moving services.\nL91: \nL92: Mailing Services\nL93: \nL94: cite19†Go to Mailing Services L95: DTMB Mail and Delivery Services offers a full range of automated and manual mail handling and delivery services.\nL96: \nL97: Printing Services\nL98: \nL99: cite20†Go to Printing Services L100: \nL101: Innovative solutions to your state printing needs.\nL102: \nL103: Real Estate Services\nL104: \nL105: cite21†Go to Real Estate Services L106: \nL107: The DTMB Real Estate Division provides real estate and occupancy services for State of Michigan agency needs.\nL108: \nL109: Records Management Services\nL110: \nL111: cite22†Go to Records Management Services L112: Information and services for local government agencies about managing records and data in the most effective, cost efficient, and legally compliant manner.\nL113: \nL114: Risk Management\nL115: \nL116: cite23†Go to Risk Management L117: \nL118: The State of Michigan’s Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) section is responsible for insuring and protecting the people, property, and activities of state government.\nL119: \nL120:   * cite24†State Agency Requests for Insurance Coverage & Other ERM Services L121: \nL122: Shop Surplus!\nL123: \nL124: cite25†Go to Shop Surplus! L125: Details on state surplus property, auctions, and eligibility for federal surplus programs.\nL126: \nL127: SUITE\nL128: \nL129: cite26†Go to SUITE L130: \nL131: The purpose of SUITE is to ensure consistent process usage throughout the State of Michigan.  SUITE is based on industry best practices.\nL132: \nL133:   * cite27†Information Technology (IT) Investment Fund Portfolio Report L134: \nL135: Travel\nL136: \nL137: cite28†Go to Travel L138: \nL139: Information for state employees and vendors, including hotel listings, travel rates, forms, and regulations.\nL140: \nL141: Procurement\nL142: \nL143: cite29†Go to Procurement L144: Design & Construction Division\nL145: \nL146: cite30†Go to Design & Construction Division L147: \nL148: Design & Construction Information\nL149: \nL150: Contract Connect\nL151: \nL152: cite31†Go to Contract Connect L153: \nL154: The Contract Connect website provides info to vendors interested in doing business with the State of Michigan. Contract Connect is managed by State of Michigan Procurement.\nL155: \nL156: MiDEAL\nL157: \nL158: cite32†Go to MiDEAL L159: \nL160: MiDEAL\nL161: \nL162: Facilities\nL163: \nL164: cite33†Go to Facilities L165: \nL166: Building and Parking Services\nL167: \nL168: cite34†Go to Building and Parking Services L169: \nL170: Design and Construction Division\nL171: Real Estate Services\nL172: \nL173: Careers\nL174: \nL175: Contact\nL176: \nL177: cite35†Go to Conta